# This is a SECOND, separate .env file — for `docker compose` variable
# substitution only (docker-compose.yml, build args). It lives here in the
# repo checkout and is different from the runtime .env described in
# .env.example, which lives outside the repo at $SYNAPSE_HOST_DIR/.env and is
# mounted into the container via env_file.
#
# Copy this to `.env` in the repo root before running `docker compose` or
# `update.sh` on a Docker/QNAP deployment.

# Absolute path to your persistent data volume on the Docker host — the
# parent directory containing notes/, synapse-engine/, credentials/, ssh/,
# and data/. Example for a QNAP NAS: /share/YOUR_VOLUME/synapse
SYNAPSE_HOST_DIR=/path/to/synapse

# Optional: git identity used for commits the container makes to your notes
# vault. Defaults to a generic bot identity if unset.
# GIT_USER_NAME=Your Name
# GIT_USER_EMAIL=you@example.com
